Alessandro Saiani.

This repository is DUAL-LICENSED. Which of the two licenses applies to a given
package is listed below and in docs/LICENSING.md; each published NuGet package
includes the full text of its applicable license:

  • Foundation, capabilities & tooling  →  MIT
    (see licenses/LICENSE-MIT.txt)
    Free for everyone, forever — including production and commercial use, at any
    scale. Covers: Result, Ensure, Abstractions, Specification, Validation,
    Mapping, Caching, Patch, Temporal, Internationalization, Resilience,
    Configuration, Logging, FeatureFlags, Discovery, Storage, Testing, and the
    SourceGenerator.

  • Framework runtime (the value)  →  PolyForm Small Business 1.0.0
    (see licenses/LICENSE-PolyForm-Small-Business-1.0.0.txt)
    Free for small businesses (under US $1,000,000 annual revenue AND under 100
    employees/contractors), plus personal, educational, and open-source use. A
    commercial license is required above that threshold. Covers the
    domain-driven runtime and the composed-framework experience (Persistence,
    Actions, Endpoints, Composition, Events, Messaging, Jobs, Migrations,
    Identity, Authorization, MultiTenancy, ControlPlane, Client, the Medium
    Blocks, the Documents & media packages, the compliance packages (Audit,
    Privacy, Cryptography, Redaction, Incidents), and the Platform preview).

There is no conversion clause and no time-bomb: code the generator emits into
your project is yours and keeps working.

Plain-language summary, the full package map, and commercial-license terms:

    docs/LICENSING.md

NOTE (preview): a legal review of this dual-licensing setup is recommended
before the first public release.
